{
  "adventure": {
    "pitch": "A gothic tale of drowned debt: the mining town of Hollowmere was flooded to make a reservoir, sealing bell-founder Corvin Bell inside his own half-finished church. His masterwork bronze bell went down with him. Now, every night the bell tolls beneath the water and rises a little higher on its rope, and with each toll the drowned dead climb the rope toward the living. The debt owed him must be paid",
    "scenes": {
      "scene:b1": {
        "title": "The Rope on the Shore",
        "summary": "The party arrives at a shore hamlet of stilted shacks as the bell's first muffled toll shudders through the water. Fisherfolk cower behind barred doors; the boatwright Mother Sedge knows the old story. A slick bell-rope rises from the deep and is anchored to a stone weir. Investigate the rope (Perception DC 12 finds fresh drowned handprints climbing it), calm or bargain with Sedge (Persuasion DC 13 gets a boat and the drowned town's map), or hold the shore when the night's first climbers crest the water. Waterlogged dead haul themselves ashore at the toll.",
        "exits": [
          "scene:b2"
        ],
        "scenePlan": {
          "look": "A pebbled crescent shore under a stone weir; stilted shacks lean over black water, jetties jut into the reservoir, and a thick tarred rope climbs from the deep to an iron ring on the weir.",
