      "scene:b3": {
        "title": "The Founder in His Bell",
        "summary": "Inside the drowned church, the great bronze bell hangs mouth-down over the founder's sealed tomb; within it, wound in the rope, is Corvin Bell \u2014 a bloated, ringing revenant who tolls the dead upward with his own bones. Confront him. He can be laid to rest by returning the clapper and tolling the bell once in true mourning (Religion/Persuasion DC 15 acknowledges his debt), or destroyed outright (harder fight, curse lingers). Elara may read the founder's inscription (Arcana DC 14) revealing the toll is a debt-count, not malice. Aldric can brace the swinging bell against him. End it as the bell rings clean and the water stills.",
