  "blueprint": {
    "premise": "A gothic tale of drowned debt: the mining town of Hollowmere was flooded to make a reservoir, sealing bell-founder Corvin Bell inside his own half-finished church. His masterwork bronze bell went down with him. Now, every night the bell tolls beneath the water and rises a little higher on its rope, and with each toll the drowned dead climb the rope toward the living. The debt owed him must be paid",
    "centralProblem": "The bell rises nightly, dragging the reservoir's dead upward; unless the party descends to the drowned church and settles the founder's debt (his body given rest, his bell's tongue silenced or restored), the flood-dead will overrun the shore hamlet.",
    "intendedEnding": "The party reaches the sunken church, confronts the animate remains of Corvin Bell, and pays his debt \u2014 burying his bones, returning the stolen bell-clapper to hang the bell true, and tolling it once in honest mourning. The bell falls silent, the risen dead sink back, and the reservoir stills. If they merely destroy him, the tolling stops but the valley remains cursed water.",
    "opening": "Dusk on the shingle shore of Weirwater Reservoir, at the drowned hamlet of Hollowmere, where a rotted bell-rope trails up out of the black water onto the beach \u2014 and something has been climbing it.",
    "spine": [
      {
        "milestone": "The Toll Begins",
        "intent": "Party learns the bell rises and the dead climb its rope.",
        "sceneId": "scene:b1"
      },
      {
        "milestone": "The Stolen Clapper",
        "intent": "Party recovers the tool needed to pay the debt.",
        "sceneId": "scene:b2"
      },
      {
        "milestone": "The Debt Settled",
        "intent": "Founder laid to rest, bell rung true.",
        "sceneId": "scene:b3"
      },
      {
        "milestone": "The Still Water",
        "intent": "The reservoir falls silent; the drowned sink home and the valley is finally at peace."
      }
    ]
  },
